WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.250
A doorway.

2
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:05.390
Beside it, a bright fountain,
splashing over the step.

3
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:10.100
For Wordsworth's speaker, a friend's
love was once a fountain like this.

4
00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.520
Then: "There is a change".

5
00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:14.120
He says he is poor.

6
00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:15.840
The fountain is gone.

7
00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:20.840
In its place stands a dark,
round well, its lid half closed.

8
00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:22.960
A fountain, then a well.

9
00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:24.850
So why is that so bad?

10
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.810
In this mission, you'll meet a close
friendship that has quietly changed,

11
00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:31.030
in a poem from 1807.

12
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:35.240
You'll follow one extended
metaphor, from fountain to well.

13
00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:38.120
And you'll hear how the
poem ends, hesitant,

14
00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:40.160
with dashes and questions.

15
00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:45.180
Your mission: explain why the change
from fountain to well is so bad.
